+An out-of-bounds access (in C99 complex lowering) could occur when
+lowering casts or arithmetic on a complex type whose element type is
+an extended floating-point type (_Float16, _Float32, _Float64, or
+_Float128).  For example, with --gnu_version=160100 --c++23:
