+(8 bits for char types, 16 bits for short types, etc.) as if they are fields
+of that type.  That type might be different from the type the bit field is
+declared with.  In the example above, the bit field is declared as "unsigned",
+but the type of s.u is "unsigned char" (the signedness is carried over).
+Thus, the output of this program is "uchar".  The front end now emulates that
+behavior.
+```
