+The default behavior can be overridden using the new
+--[no_]relaxed_abstract_checking command-line option.  For example, with
+--relaxed_abstract_checking:
+
+  struct A { virtual void f() = 0; };
+  A f0(A);     // Previously an error for return and parameter, now okay
+  A f1(A a) {  // Previously and still an error for return and parameter types
+    f0(a);     // Now an error for return and parameter types
+    return a;
+  }
+```
