+## 5/31/19 · `EDGpcfe/21158`
+
+**GNU/Clang compatibility: Mutability of compound literals**  
+*C-score +4; hits: in c, compound literal*
+
+```text
+
+In GNU and Clang modes, the front end sometimes treats compound literals as
+rvalues.  Those rvalues may later be turned back into lvalues by associating
+them with a generated static variable.  That variable was previously declared
+with the type specified for the compound literal, but now it is always declared
+with a "const" type to communicate the immutability of the compound literal
+(the expression denoting the compound literal is not necessarily "const",
+however).  Note that the standard (in C) "compound literal" feature produces
+an lvalue that is mutable if its type is not "const".
