+## 5/2/19 · `EDGcpfe/21186`
+
+**GNU compatibility: Suppress __weak__ attribute with __always_inline__**  
+*C-score +3; hits: gnu c, inline*
+
+```text
+
+When a routine is marked for a COMDAT section the C-generating back end
+(when GCC or Clang is being used as the back end compiler) adds the __weak__
+attribute to the generated C declaration.  For later versions of GCC, that
+can cause the generated code to fail to compile when the routine is also marked
+with the __always_inline__ attribute (because the linker could conceivably
+choose a different routine than the one that is inlined in the translation
+unit).  In such cases, the __weak__ attribute is now suppressed.  For example:
