+## 12/7/11 · `EDGcpfe/12313`
+
+**Position of aggregate initializers**  
+*C-score +3; hits: initializer, aggregate*
+
+```text
+
+The front end now records the position of aggregate initializers in the
+corresponding ck_aggregate entry's source_corresp.decl_position field.  It
+does so both for top-level aggregate initializers (which are always brace-
+enclosed) and for sub-aggregate initializers (which may or may not be brace-
+enclosed).  If the ck_aggregate entry represents a brace-enclosed initializer,
+the recorded position is that of the opening brace; if it represents an
+initializer not enclosed in braces, the position of the first element in the
+initializer is recorded instead.  For example:
