+name.  However, if a function or variable name appeared both as a regular name
+and as an asm name, the alias was previously resolved to the entity with the
+asm name.  This could later trigger warnings or errors if that entity did not
+have a definition.  Now, the alias resolution method gives precedence to the
+entity with a definition.  For example (GNU C mode):
